---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import siteConfig from '@/site-config'
---

<BaseLayout description={siteConfig.description}>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1 class="text-title">Hi, I'm Shad Mirza</h1>
    <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">Senior Software Engineer • DigitalOcean GenAI • ~8 years</p>

    <p>
      I build AI platform surfaces, observability, and agent-quality systems at DigitalOcean. Before that I spent years
      shipping high-scale product and mobile at Hashnode (130M+ monthly API requests, 160K+ MAUs).
    </p>

    <p>
      <img width="640" height="360" src="/hero.jpg" alt="Shad Mirza - Senior Software Engineer" />
    </p>

    <h2>What I Do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>GenAI platform:</strong> Product APIs, day-0 model launches, and batch inference for builders on DigitalOcean
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Observability:</strong> OpenTelemetry across GenAI clusters, customer metrics/logs under load, and playbooks
        other teams can run without me
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Agent systems:</strong> Agent feedback, evaluation loops, and tooling that help teams measure quality
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Reusable DX:</strong> Cursor skills and short written docs that turn hard-won ops knowledge into self-serve
        defaults
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Selected Impact</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Shipped day-one Claude and OpenAI model integrations within hours of public announcement, matching top-tier
        cloud time-to-market
      </li>
      <li>
        Architected Unified Batch Inference; built the API server, migration, and LiteLLM proxy integration to rescue an
        at-risk launch, and wrote the
        <a href="https://www.digitalocean.com/blog/introducing-batch-inference" target="_blank"
          >DigitalOcean launch post</a
        >
      </li>
      <li>
        Built GenAI observability from scratch (OpenTelemetry across clusters, customer metrics/logs), including fixing
        collector OOMs by tuning batches from 10,000 to 1,000 with memory limiters and retries
      </li>
      <li>
        Turned multi-hour ops setup into self-serve Cursor skills and playbooks other teams run without me; open-sourced
        <a href="https://github.com/iamshadmirza/to-onepager" target="_blank">to-onepager</a>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>My Expertise</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Platform & APIs:</strong> TypeScript, Go, Node.js, GraphQL, REST, serverless and service-oriented designs
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>AI platform:</strong> Inference APIs, batch jobs, proxy/auth boundaries, agent feedback and evaluation loops
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Cloud & ops:</strong> Kubernetes/DOKS, OpenTelemetry, AWS (Lambda, API Gateway, Step Functions, EventBridge,
        S3, SQS/SNS), Infrastructure as Code (SST, CDK)
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Product surfaces:</strong> React, React Native, Next.js, CI/CD, TDD
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Recent Experience</h2>
    <p>
      Currently a <strong>Senior Software Engineer</strong> at DigitalOcean GenAI (since Nov 2025): AI Platform first, then
      agent feedback and evaluation. I ship platform APIs customers can use on day one, make GenAI clusters observable under
      load, and build the loops that measure agent quality.
    </p>

    <p>
      Previously at <strong>Hashnode</strong> as Platform Engineer and Mobile App Lead: AWS serverless GraphQL (130M+ requests/month),
      GitHub-synced docs, an AI documentation assistant (OpenAI, LangChain, Pinecone), and a React Native app built from
      scratch (50K MAUs, 36% rating lift, 60% fewer crash reports). Mentored 5+ engineers.
    </p>

    <p>
      Earlier at <strong>Sheevoot Int Pvt. Ltd.</strong> as a Mobile Application Engineer on Easebuoy (ride/food/car wash),
      supporting 10K+ MAUs with Maps integrations and vendor ops apps.
    </p>

    <h2>Open Source & Writing</h2>
    <p>I write and ship tools when a pattern repeats. Highlights:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/iamshadmirza/to-onepager" target="_blank">to-onepager</a> (Cursor skill for grounded
        one-pagers)
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="https://github.com/iamshadmirza/react-native-design-system" target="_blank"
          >React Native design system</a
        >
      </li>
      <li>
        Writing for
        <a href="https://www.digitalocean.com/blog/introducing-batch-inference" target="_blank">DigitalOcean</a>,
        <a href="https://engineering.hashnode.com/" target="_blank">Hashnode Engineering</a>,
        <a href="https://blog.logrocket.com/react-native-draggable-flatlist/" target="_blank">LogRocket</a>,
        <a href="https://soshace.com/author/iamshadmirza/" target="_blank">Soshace</a>, and
        <a href="https://alligator.io" target="_blank">Alligator.io</a>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <hr class="hr-line" />

    <h2>Let's Connect</h2>
    <p>Find me on</p>
    <p class="flex gap-x-4 gap-y-2 flex-wrap">
      {
        siteConfig.socialLinks.map((link) => (
          <a aria-label={link.text} href={link.href} target="_blank" class="prose-link flex items-center gap-2">
            <i class:list={[link.icon]} />
            {link.text}
          </a>
        ))
      }
    </p>

    <p>
      For collaborations, opportunities, or a hello, email
      <a prose-link aria-label={siteConfig.email} href={`mailto:${siteConfig.email}`}>
        {siteConfig.email}
      </a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
